  a kind row whole (covenant_cut_at_sinai): {'en': "the covenant cut at Sinai — 'and He said: behold I cut a covenant, before all your people I will do wonders which have not been created in all the earth', 'and the LORD said to Moses: write for yourself these words, for by the mouth of these words I have cut a covenant with you and with Israel': the covenant with the thirteen attributes that never returns empty (Rosh Hashanah 17b:7), and the TWO CHANNELS' medium law from one verse — written things you may not say by heart, oral things you may not put in writing (Gittin 60b:5), the Torah mostly oral by R. Yochanan's reading of 'by the mouth' (60b:2), the covenant cut for the sake of the oral (60b:6)", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי כֹּרֵת בְּרִית נֶגֶד כָּל עַמְּךָ אֶעֱשֶׂה נִפְלָאֹת (and He said: behold I cut a covenant, before all your people I will do wonders — Exod 34:10); כְּתָב לְךָ אֶת הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה כִּי עַל פִּי הַ
